8\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. We know that $y=-1$ is a solution to $f(y)=0,$ and so $(y+1)$ is a factor of the polynomial $f(y).$ Dividing $f(y)$ by $(y+1)$ using synthetic division, we get\n\n|  | ${y}^{3}$ | ${y}^{2}$ | ${y}^{1}$ | ${y}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\n \nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =(y+1)({y}^{2}+2y+1) \\\\  & =(y+1)(y+1)^{2} \\\\  & =(y+1)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(y)$ has exactly one equilibrium solution,\n\n$$\ny(t)=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307420 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307421 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307422 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307423 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307424 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1041 "selection" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307422 13194139534748 true] [17592186307419 1110 #uuid "b562362d-d7ce-506e-ae1c-000c72790521" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307420 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307420 1111 #uuid "dcc12c51-ee79-58d2-877c-7faad905b73f" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307421 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307421 1111 #uuid "c0931547-c610-536e-b878-0a51ca26d72c" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307422 1034 "I only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307422 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307422 1111 #uuid "38b5b4c7-9730-56bc-86f6-6204aa6f2013" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307423 1034 "III only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319413953