xists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2},\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2}.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)=(1)^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{e}^{2}=-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=e$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(e)={e}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-{e}^{2}={e}^{2}-{e}^{2}=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307443 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307444 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307445 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307446 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307447 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1041 "selection" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307447 13194139534748 true] [17592186307442 1110 #uuid "d9dd7a4c-1cc7-5eb6-8a4e-7db340840978" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307443 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307443 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307443 1111 #uuid "7ae1623f-993c-52c1-a93a-7f56da345322" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307444 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307444 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307444 1111 #uuid "835094d4-de03-56d8-be93-f2dc08f155f4" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307445 1034 "I only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307445 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307445 1111 #uuid "2e830bf7-8ee9-5078-b729-f3a169db3a9d" 13194