454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307449 1110 #uuid "eeb3b0d8-ac57-5640-8baf-5fc9b36cc574" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307450 1034 "${y}_{1}(x)=-6$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=9$" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307450 1111 #uuid "bb3c5315-0f06-5f4b-8850-479f72682ca8" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307451 1034 "${y}_{1}(x)=0$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=1$" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307451 1111 #uuid "870a9709-a298-53cd-8ed5-d6a4fe0620a6" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307452 1034 "${y}_{1}(x)=0$ only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307452 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307452 1111 #uuid "e93a18f6-875f-5686-a86e-3517e0d36260" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307453 1034 "${y}_{1}(x)=6$ only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307453 1111 #uuid "05b97d97-7d4c-51eb-a6dc-ff9b23e33d15" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307454 1034 "${y}_{1}(x)=3$ only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307454 1111 #uuid "179488ee-017d-5d74-b45a-8ecf76a4b479" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307456 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1089 "q-96174" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1100 "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}={y}^{3}-7{y}^{2}+15y-9.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=3$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation\n- $y=-1$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation\n- The equation has $2$ distinct equilibrium solutions" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1113 #uuid "2c60a39c-067b-5ec0-8cd6-367f8fd5b1e2" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307455 1145 "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(t)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is a equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nIn our case, we have that $f(y)={y}^{3}-7{y}^{2}+15y-9.$\n\nLet's examine the statement one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true.  We have that $f(3)=(3)^{3}-7(3)^{2}+15(3)-9=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false.  We have that $f(-1)=(-1)^{3}-7(-1)^{2}+15(-1)-9=-32\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. We know that $y=3$ is a solution to $f(y)=0,$ and so $(y-3)$ is a factor of the polynomial $f(y).$ Dividing $f(y)$ by $(y-3)$ using synthetic division, we get\n\n|  | ${y}^{3}$ | ${y}^{2}$ | ${y}^{1}$ | ${y}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $-7$ | $15$ | $-9$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-12$ | $9$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-4$ | $3$ | $0$ |\n\n \nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =(y-3)({y}^{2}-4y+3) \\\\  & =(y-3)(y-1)(y-3) \\\\  & =(y-1)(y-3)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(y)$ has $2$ distinct equilibrium solutions, \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(t)=1,\\,{y}_{2}(t)=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307457 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307458 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307459 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307460 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307461 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1041 "selection" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307459 13194139534748 true] [17592186307456 1110 #uuid "dcd9c747-c267-58a2-905c-9844ba7f534c" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307457 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307457 1111 #uuid "5793135a-3e27-5572-9818-332f9eb36d36" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307458 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534748 true] [17592186307458 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534748 true] [17592186307458 1111 #uuid "edadb0a5-e119-59a6-a71a-d0ab8a5b824c" 1319413953